MoonBit allows for a local module dependency (that is, a module not uploaded to mooncakes). It's mentioned in the detailed [module configuration docs](https://docs.moonbitlang.com/en/latest/toolchain/moon/module.html). Unfortunately, I was only able to find that after failing to learn it from the [package manager tour](https://docs.moonbitlang.com/en/latest/toolchain/moon/package-manage-tour.html) or `moon add --help`, then failing to find instructions in the GitHub issues or the discord logs. Maybe the feature is intentionally obscure. Regardless, here is an example for others who failed like me.

The syntax in your `moon.mod.json` file is as follows:

```json
  "deps": {
    "foo/bar": {
      "path": "../../path/to/foo-module"
    },
  },
```

Once that dependency is declared, a `moon.pkg.json` file can refer to that module as `"foo/bar"`:

```json
  "import": [
    {
      "path": "foo/bar",
      "alias": "bar"
    }
  ],
```

